      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "There are **three ways** to change a `<span>`'s color on mouse over: using **CSS**, **inline HTML events**, or **JavaScript**. Here they are:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 1: CSS `:hover` (Recommended)\n\nThis is the simplest and cleanest approach.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <style>\n    span {\n      color: black;\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n\n    span:hover {\n      color: red;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <span>Hover over me!</span>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
