  "answer_text": "There are **three ways** to change a `<span>`'s color on mouse over: using **CSS**, **inline HTML events**, or **JavaScript**. Here they are:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 1: CSS `:hover` (Recommended)\n\nThis is the simplest and cleanest approach.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <style>\n    span {\n      color: black;\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n\n    span:hover {\n      color: red;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <span>Hover over me!</span>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nIf you need to change the text color on mouseover for all elements of a certain type, then using CSS is the best option.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: Inline `onmouseover` / `onmouseout` HTML Attributes\n\nYou can handle it directly in the HTML tag using event attributes:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<body>\n  <span\n    onmouseover=\"this.style.color='red'\"\n    onmouseout=\"this.style.color='black'\">\n    Hover over me!\n  </span>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n- `onmouseover` \u2014 fires when the mouse pointer enters the element.\n- `onmouseout` \u2014 fires when the mouse pointer leaves the element, resetting the color.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 3: JavaScript `addEventListener`\n\nIf you need to change the text color on mouseover for a specific element, or if you need to change the text color dynamically, then using JavaScript is the best option.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<body>\n  <span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n  <script>\n    const mySpan = document.getElementById('mySpan');\n\n    mySpan.addEventListener('mouseover', function () {\n      mySpan.style.color = 'red';\n    });\n\n    mySpan.addEventListener('mouseout', function () {\n      mySpan.style.color = 'black';\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nA `mouseover` event is added to the element, changing its text color when the user hovers over it. A `mouseout` event is also added to change its text color back to the default when the user moves their cursor out.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfc6 Which method should you use?\n\n| Method | Best For |\n|---|---|\n| **CSS `:hover`** | Simple, static color changes \u2014 cleanest & most efficient |\n| **Inline HTML** | Quick prototyping or very simple cases |\n| **JavaScript** | Dynamic or conditional color changes at runtime |\n\nIn most cases, **CSS `:hover`** is the recommended approach as it keeps styling separate from logic and requires no JavaScript.",
